  "finding": "The shipped scorecard never exceeds grade 4, while the rounded panel mean does reach 5 (112 cells) and 6 (9 cells). The compression is not a rounding artefact: the continuous predictions themselves are pulled toward the middle, so the model systematically under-predicts high-intensity samples and slightly over-predicts low ones. This is a genuine limitation of predicting a panel mean from chemistry with MAE ~0.45 on a 0-6 scale, and it must be reported rather than hidden.",
